@startuml
title SplitSmart System Context (Complete product; Swing MVP is separate)
left to right direction

actor "Individual user" as User
actor "Group organizer" as Organizer
actor "Expense approver" as Approver
rectangle "Web client" as Web
rectangle "Android client" as Android
rectangle "iOS client" as IOS
rectangle "Java Swing MVP client\n(separate implementation slice)" as Swing
rectangle "Shared authenticated\nSplitSmart services\n(proposed complete product)" as Services
database "Shared authorized records\n(proposed)" as Data
rectangle "Email / push provider\n(optional, unselected)" as Channels

User --> Web
User --> Android
User --> IOS
User --> Swing
Organizer --> Web
Approver --> Web
Web --> Services
Android --> Services
IOS --> Services
Swing --> Services : only if collaborative MVP approved
Services --> Data
Services --> Channels : only if channels approved

note bottom of Swing
  Swing alone does not meet the customer requirement for
  primarily web-based, Android and iOS access.
end note
@enduml
